<section class="lp-sec"><div class="lp-pgrid"><div class="lp-pc feat" data-anim="" data-delay="0"><div class="art"></div><div class="body"><span class="tag">Principle</span><p>“No fixed denominations, no mixer queues, no waiting periods. <span class="dim">Any amount, whenever you want it back.</span>”</p><div class="who"><span><b>Pool design</b>2-in / 2-out shielded notes with change</span></div></div></div><div class="lp-pc" data-anim="" data-delay="1"><span class="tag">Principle</span><p>“Your signature derives everything, on your device. <span class="dim">It never leaves your browser, every proof is built locally, and nothing that can spend your notes is stored.</span>”</p><div class="who"><span><b>Non-custodial</b>Pools are contracts; nothing that can spend your notes is stored</span></div></div><div class="lp-pc" data-anim="" data-delay="2"><span class="tag">Principle</span><p>“The relayer pays the gas, <span class="dim">so the paying wallet is never yours.</span>”</p><div class="who"><span><b>Relayed transactions</b>The relayer only sees finished proofs; a flat fee comes from the note itself</span></div></div><div class="lp-pc" data-anim="" data-delay="0"><span class="tag">Principle</span><p>“Bridges should not know who is on the other side. <span class="dim">Intents keep the recipient off the origin chain.</span>”</p><div class="who"><span><b>NEAR Intents routing</b>One-off solver deposit address per transfer</span></div></div><div class="lp-pc" data-anim="" data-delay="1"><span class="tag">Principle</span><p>“If a step fails, the money is still yours. <span class="dim">Every burner and bridge is recoverable from any device.</span>”</p><div class="who"><span><b>Recovery from any device</b>Burner keys encrypted client-side, bridges tracked to the end</span></div></div></div></section>
